  "body": "What happens: The Sinumerik post writes `P<ms>` on G83 in ISO mode. The G83 P word is not verified for that control. The control may ignore it or raise an alarm, so the dwell at the machine may differ from the user's setting.\n\nExpected: The post writes a G83 dwell only in a form that the control's published format supports. Otherwise the post refuses the dwell by name with a diagnostic.\n\nEvidence: `assets/posts/sinumerik.cps:725`. Found by the review of PR #2048: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2048#issuecomment-6950568559\n\nPriority: P1. An unverified word can make the posted program run differently from the user's setting (wrong posted G-code).\n\nRelated: #1820 covers the same question for the Fanuc-family posts.\n\nDone means: The Sinumerik post writes a G83 dwell only in a verified form, or refuses it by name. A test pins the output.\n",
